  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: use-after-free in the bz2 and lzma incremental\n     decompressors when a memory allocation failure leaves a stale input\n     pointer\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-6100.patch: reset bzs->next_in and lzs->next_in\n       to NULL on the error path of decompress() in Modules/_bz2module.c and\n       Modules/_lzmamodule.c, so a decompressor reused after a MemoryError no\n       longer reads or writes through a pointer to the already-released caller\n       buffer\n     - CVE-2026-6100",
